  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Invitational Training Program for Local Government Officials in Developing Countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This program aims to strengthen the capacity of public officials in developing countries. It does so by inviting officials and training institution leaders from partner regions engaged in international exchange and cooperation. Together, they share best practices in local governance and transfer advanced training methodologies. It also seeks to enhance the effectiveness of ODA by integrating and reflecting the ODA demands of Korean local governments. Furthermore, the program supports local diplomacy by promoting mutually beneficial, win-win cooperation (K-ODA), including the sharing of policy experiences and joint responses to common challenges through partnerships between domestic and foreign local governments. 
The program operates through tailored lectures and a curriculum designed;
  - To produce action plans (AP) directly applicable in the field
  - To enhance the capabilities of developing country officials by sharing best practices adaptable to the host country&apos;s context
  - To support sustainable development in recipient countries by driving innovation in public administration sectors, establishing relevant systems, and developing legislation.</narrative>
  </description>
